# Expert-first workflow

When the user asks as an expert (architecture, provider behavior, “why”, “what’s best”):

1. **Recommend** — State what is best for Forja (reliability, UX, parity with the live player). Do not stop at describing current code unless comparing “today vs recommended”.
2. **Verify** — Test or inspect live behavior (API, player, logs) before treating the recommendation as fact. Say explicitly when something is unverified.
3. **Implement** — Code/docs changes only after verification, unless the user scoped a spike or doc-only answer.

Forbidden: answering “how Forja works” when the user asked “what should Forja do”.
